chapter.v:
	I have 

	 stretched out My hands all day long to a rebellious people,Who walk in a way that is not good,According to their own thoughts;
 [Ps. 12:1; Is. 57:1] [Hab. 1:15]

	A people 

	 who provoke Me to anger continually to My face;Who sacrifice in gardens,And burn incense on altars of brick;
 [Amos 5:12; Mic. 3:11]

	Who sit 

	 among the graves,And spend the night in the tombs;Who eat swine’s flesh,And the broth of abominable things is in their vessels;
 [Is. 55:13; Ezek.]

	Therefore thus 

	 says the Lord God:“Behold, My servants shall eat,But you shall be hungry;Behold, My servants shall drink,But you shall be thirsty;Behold, My servants shall rejoice,But you shall be ashamed;
 [Jer. 21:14]

	You shall 

	 leave your name as a curse to My chosen;For the Lord God will slay you,And call His servants by another name;
 [Ps. 68:22; 78:12 v Ex.]
